    "objective": "Solidify the 6 colleagues supporting 32/29, and attempt to peel off 2-3 colleagues from the 65/58 camp (targeting Colleague 3, 4, or 1) by drilling into the exact definition of blocking and the canonical formulation of proportionality degree/core bounds.",
    "key_argument": "1) Reiterate total consensus on s(N, W2) = 58. 2) For s(N, W1), challenge the assumption that T can unilaterally give 9 to all 8 voters under the standard core definition when 8 common candidates are already universally approved. Emphasize why the infimum of the core is 64, yielding the canonical reduced answer 32/29."
  }
}

